#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:2
msgid "``parallel`` tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:4
msgid ""
"A **Parallel task** is defined by an array of other tasks to be run "
"concurrently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:6
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"check.parallel = [\"mypy\", \"pylint\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:11
msgid ""
"By default the contents of the array are interpreted as references to other "
"tasks (actually an inline :doc:`ref<ref>` task). However, this behaviour can "
"be altered by setting the :toml:`default_item_type` option locally on the "
"parallel task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:13
msgid ""
"Subtask outputs are forwarded to the console with a prefix identifying the "
"task, in either streaming or buffered mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:17
msgid ""
"Because subtask output is captured via a pipe rather than written directly "
"to the terminal, tools that detect terminal support by calling ``isatty()`` "
"(such as Ruff, Behave, and others) will disable colored output when run as "
"parallel subtasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:19
msgid ""
"The standard workaround is to set the ``FORCE_COLOR`` environment variable "
"on the affected subtask, which tells tools to force colored output "
"regardless of TTY detection. Poe also respects this variable for its own "
"output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:21
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.check]\n"
"parallel = [\n"
"  { cmd = \"ruff check\" },\n"
"  { cmd = \"mypy\" },\n"
"]\n"
"env = { FORCE_COLOR = \"1\" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:30
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set ``FORCE_COLOR`` at the global or project level if all "
"tasks should use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:34
msgid "Available task options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:36
msgid ""
"``parallel`` tasks support all of the :doc:`standard task options <../"
"options>` with the exception of ``use_exec`` and ``capture_stdout``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:38
msgid "The following options are also accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:40
msgid ""
"**ignore_fail** : ``bool`` | ``Literal[\"return_zero\", "
"\"return_non_zero\"]`` :ref:`📖<Continue on subtask failure>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:39
msgid "bool | Literal[\"return_zero\", \"return_non_zero\"] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:41
msgid ""
"If set to something other than false then the failure (or non-zero return "
"value) of one task in the parallel group does not abort the execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:43
msgid ""
"**default_item_type** : ``str`` :ref:`📖<Changing the default item type>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:42
#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:48
#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:54
msgid "str 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:44
msgid ""
"Change the task type that is applied to string array items in this parallel "
"group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:46
msgid ""
"**output_mode** : ``Literal[\"stream\", \"buffer\"]`` :ref:`📖<Buffer "
"subtask output>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:45
msgid "Literal[\"stream\", \"buffer\"] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:47
msgid ""
"Controls how subtask stdout is handled. The default ``stream`` mode outputs "
"each line as it arrives, while ``buffer`` keeps each task's stdout grouped "
"together and prints it when the task subprocess completes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:49
msgid "**prefix** : ``str`` :ref:`📖<Customize output prefixing>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:50
msgid ""
"Set the prefix applied to each line of output from subtasks. By default this "
"is the task name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:52
msgid "**prefix_max** : ``int`` :ref:`📖<Customize output prefixing>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:51
msgid "int 📖"
msgstr "int 📖"

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:53
msgid ""
"Set the maximum width of the prefix. Longer prefixes will be truncated. "
"Default is 16 characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:55
msgid "**prefix_template** : ``str`` :ref:`📖<Customize output prefixing>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:56
msgid ""
"Specifies a template for how the prefix is applied after truncating it to "
"the prefix_max length. The default prefix_template is ``{color_start}{prefix}"
"{color_end} |``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:60
msgid "Continue on subtask failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:62
msgid ""
"A failure (non-zero result) will result in any remaining subtasks being "
"cancelled, unless the :toml:`ignore_fail` option is set on the task like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:64
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"attempts.parallel = [\"task1\", \"task2\", \"task3\"]\n"
"attempts.ignore_fail = true"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:70
msgid ""
"If you want to run all the subtasks to completion but return non-zero result "
"in the end of the parallel group if any of the subtasks have failed you can "
"set :toml:`ignore_fail` option to the :toml:`return_non_zero` like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:72
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"attempts.parallel = [\"task1\", \"task2\", \"task3\"]\n"
"attempts.ignore_fail = \"return_non_zero\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:80
msgid "Changing the default item type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:82
msgid ""
"If you want strings in the array to be interpreted as a task type other "
"than :doc:`ref<ref>` you may specify then :toml:`default_item_type` option "
"like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:84
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"check.parallel = [\n"
"  \"linters:run_mypy(all=True)\",\n"
"  \"linters:run_pylint\",\n"
"  \"linters:run_flake8\",\n"
"]\n"
"default_item_type = \"script\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:94
msgid "Alternatively you can declare other task types inline like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:96
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"check.parallel = [\n"
"  { script = \"linters:run_mypy(all=True)\" },\n"
"  { script = \"linters:run_pylint\" },\n"
"  { script = \"linters:run_flake8\" },\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:107
msgid ""
"An array within a parallel task is interpreted as a :doc:"
"`sequence<sequence>` task, so you can run certain parallel subtasks :ref:"
"`with strict ordering<Composing tasks to run in parallel>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:111
msgid "Forwarding free arguments to subtasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:113
msgid ""
"By default, free arguments passed to a parallel task are not forwarded to "
"any of its subtasks. However, they can be forwarded selectively by "
"referencing the special ``$POE_EXTRA_ARGS`` environment variable in "
"individual subtask definitions. Only subtasks that explicitly reference "
"``$POE_EXTRA_ARGS`` will receive them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:115
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`forwarding-free-arguments-via-poe-extra-args` section of the "
"args guide for details and examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:119
msgid "Buffer subtask output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:121
msgid ""
"By default a parallel task forwards each line of task output directly to the "
"console with the configured prefix, so output lines from different tasks are "
"interleaved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:123
msgid ""
"If you prefer the output from each task subprocess to print as one "
"contiguous block after it finishes, set :toml:`output_mode` to :toml:"
"`\"buffer\"`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:125
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"test-matrix.parallel = [\"test-py310\", \"test-py311\"]\n"
"test-matrix.output_mode = \"buffer\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:131
msgid ""
"In buffered mode each flushed line still receives the configured prefix, but "
"stdout is held back until the leaf task exits, fails, or is cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:133
msgid ""
"To avoid unbounded memory use, Poe keeps up to approximately 4MiB of stdout "
"per leaf task in memory. If adding another complete line would exceed that "
"limit then the current buffered lines are flushed early and buffering "
"continues with later output. Normally the buffer preserves whole lines from "
"the source. However in case a single output line exceeds the 4MiB limit, the "
"line will be broken."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:137
msgid "Redirect a subtask's output to a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:139
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`capture_stdout<Redirect task output to a file>` on an individual "
"subtask to send its output to a file instead of the console:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:141
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.checks]\n"
"parallel = [\n"
"  \"lint\",\n"
"  { cmd = \"pytest\", capture_stdout = \"pytest.log\" },\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:149
msgid ""
"The captured subtask writes its stdout to the file and is excluded from the "
"prefixed console output, while the other subtasks stream to the console as "
"usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:153
msgid "Customize output prefixing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:155
msgid ""
"When running multiple tasks in parallel a prefix is applied to each line of "
"output to identify the origin. By default the prefix includes the task name "
"and has a distinct color applied to it (6 colors in rotation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:157
msgid "Example output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:159
msgid ""
"<div class=\"highlight-sh notranslate\">\n"
"<div class=\"highlight\">\n"
"<pre id=\"codecell5\">\n"
"<span style=\"color:red\">task_1</span> | task_1 output line 1\n"
"<span style=\"color:green\">task_2</span> | task_2 output line 1\n"
"<span style=\"color:yellow\">task_3</span> | task_3 output line 1\n"
"<span style=\"color:red\">task_1</span> | task_1 output line 2\n"
"<span style=\"color:blue\">task_4</span> | task_4 output line 1\n"
"<span style=\"color:yellow\">task_3</span> | task_3 output line 2\n"
"<span style=\"color:magenta\">task_5</span> | task_5 output line 1\n"
"<span style=\"color:cyan\">task_6</span> | task_6 output line 1\n"
"</pre>\n"
"</div>\n"
"</div>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:176
msgid "This behavior is customizable with the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:178
msgid ""
"Setting the ``prefix`` changes the prefix content: default ``{name}``. The "
"``{index}`` tag is also available which indicates the index of the subtask "
"within the parallel array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:179
msgid ""
"Setting the ``prefix_max`` changes the maximum width of the prefix: default "
"``16``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:180
msgid ""
"Setting the ``prefix_template`` changes how the prefix is formatted: default "
"``{color_start}{prefix}{color_end} |``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:182
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:184
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"parallel = [\"build\", \"test\", \"deploy-to-prod\"]\n"
"prefix = \"{index}:{name}\"\n"
"prefix_max = 10\n"
"prefix_template = \"[{prefix}] \""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:192
msgid "will result in output rendered like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:194
msgid ""
"[1:build] first task output line\n"
"[2:test] second task output line\n"
"[3:deploy_…] third task output line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:200
msgid "Note that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:202
msgid ""
"When the ``{prefix}`` portion of the tempalate is longer that the configured "
"``prefix_max`` then it is truncated with ellipsis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:203
msgid ""
"omitting the ``{color_start}`` and ``{color_end}`` tags from the template "
"disables prefix coloring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/task_types/parallel.rst:207
msgid ""
"If :ref:`capture_stdout<Redirect task output to a file>` is set on a subtask "
"then its output will of course be excluded."
msgstr ""
